{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh heard.</b> They informed against him (Shemot Rabbah 1)." "<b>And he sought to kill Moses.</b> He handed him over to the executioner to kill him, but the sword had no power over him (ibid.) — this is what Moses said: ״וַיַּצִּילֵנִי מֵחֶרֶב פַּרְעֹה״ (Exodus 18:4)." "(<b>And he settled in the land of Midian.</b> He tarried there — as in: ״וַיֵּשֶׁב יַעֲקֹב״ (Genesis 37).)" "<b>And he sat by the well.</b> A term of sitting. Learn from Jacob that his match came to him from the well (Shemot Rabbah 1)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:16.846628058Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}